PART VI — FILE HANDLING, INTEGRATION, AND OPERATIONS
14. AL11 and Application Server File Handling

Create a detailed organizational standard for file-based SAP developments.

Use the following proposed directory structure as the starting point:

/sys/<STREAM>/<WRICEF_ID>/<DATA_CATEGORY>/

Example:

/interface_dev/ds4/r2r/e0118/

The intended logical structure is:

data — input and working data files.
archive — successfully processed or retained files.
error — rejected files and files requiring correction.
log — processing logs and diagnostic information.

Provide a complete example:

/interface_dev/ds4/r2r/e0118/data/

/interface_dev/ds4/r2r/e0118/archive/

/interface_dev/ds4/r2r/e0118/error/

/interface_dev/ds4/r2r/e0118/log/

This is a proposed example, not an existing McCormick production path.

Important technical distinction

AL11 is used to inspect application-server directories; it is not itself a file-storage service or a directory creation mechanism.

Validate the proposed path structure against McCormick's actual SAP landscape, Basis standards, operating-system paths, and available application-server configuration.

Do not assume that a developer can create arbitrary directories or that the same physical path is used across DS4, DS5, quality, and production systems.

